## Conversation
The parent requested vendoring the independently reviewed TorchSpec DFlash2 correctness fixes into the d9b7c24 ARM64 image series.

## Actions
Applied the reviewed five-file diff after the MSC, Mooncake, and SGLang patches; verified strict conversion-key allowlists, target/draft width validation, serving scalar validation, runtime-specific input scale handling, and pytorch_model.bin warm starts; then ran focused tests and Ruff.

## Errors & Mistakes
The independent reviewer found that final_logit_softcapping=inf remained a NaN path after the first draft. Finite-positive validation and 0/inf regression cases were added before this vendor patch was generated.

## Dead Ends
Allowing conversion to continue after missing or unexpected keys was rejected because it can publish randomly initialized selector or convolution tensors. A broad missing-key allowlist was also rejected.

## Hints for Future Agents
No unexpected conversion keys are allowed. Missing embed_tokens.weight is allowed only when target_model_path replaces it. Missing t2d/d2t is allowed only during vocabulary pruning. SGLang cannot consume non-unit input_embedding_scale; vLLM can.

## Codebase Discoveries
The DFlash2 draft reuses the target embedding and LM head directly, so hidden widths must match. Trainer serving saves use pytorch_model.bin while offline conversion uses model.safetensors; warm starts now support both strictly.

## Open Questions
Selector objective convergence, composite metric fidelity, selector normalization, CUDA backward, multi-rank resume, runtime load, and GLM acceptance length remain runtime gates rather than resolved by this patch.
